From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:15:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/38] fs: sharedfs: notification queue

A second virtqueue, device to driver. The driver keeps 64 buffers
posted; the host fills one per change it made to the index because of
something that happened on the host side. The driver raises the matching
fsnotify event in the guest, so a watcher in the guest sees a host-side
save, delete or rename exactly as it would see a local one, and keeps the
affected inode current: attributes from the index, link count cleared on
delete, and, until file data is shared by reference, the page cache
dropped on modify so the next read fetches again. OVERFLOW drops the
dentry cache. The superblock registers with the session when its root is
made and deregisters when its data is dropped, under the session's lock,
so delivery never races teardown.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
